{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## `make worktree` is currently broken outright — reproduced, root cause below\n\nReporting rather than acting: this ticket is held `in_progress` by another session, and the defect sits inside the comment block this ticket's own fix introduced. Flagging it so the owner can fold it in rather than opening a competing change.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```\n$ make worktree name=repro-test-ce66 dir=/tmp/nonexistent-should-fail-early\n/bin/sh: branch: No such file or directory\nmake: *** [worktree] Error 1\n```\n\nIt fails identically regardless of arguments, so the target does not work at all right now. Two remediation agents in this session hit it and fell back to manual `git worktree add` plus `make venv && make install`.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe recipe opens a backslash-continued shell command:\n\n```make\n\t@set -e; \\\n\t@# Default is ~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>, NOT a sibling of the checkout.\n\t@# A sibling default resolves to the home directory for a clone at ~/rebar,\n\t...\n\ttarget_dir=\"$(if $(dir),$(dir),$$HOME/worktrees/rebar/$(name))\"; \\\n```\n\n`@` suppresses echo only at the start of a **recipe line**. Once the line is continued with `\\`, everything that follows is part of the same shell command, so those `@#` lines are handed to `/bin/sh` as ordinary text rather than treated as comments.\n\nThe shell then parses `<branch>` in the first such line as an input redirection from a file named `branch`, which does not exist. Hence the exact error, and hence its independence from the arguments passed.\n\n### Why it appeared now\n\nThe affected comment block is the one explaining this ticket's own change — it cites `rebar ticket 9b4a-89fb-3328-497e` by name and documents the `$HOME/worktrees/rebar/<branch>` default. The literal `<branch>` inside that explanation is what the shell redirects on.\n\nThere is a neat irony worth recording: the block immediately above it documents bug `1738`, where steps joined with `;` let a failed `make venv` pass unnoticed, and `set -e` was added to fix it. The `set -e` is what turned this into a hard abort, which is the correct behaviour — it surfaced the breakage immediately instead of handing back a half-provisioned worktree.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nMove those explanatory lines **above** the `@set -e; \\` line so make treats them as recipe comments, or convert them to `#`-prefixed shell comments **inside** the continued command with each line terminated by `; \\`. Avoid literal `<` and `>` in any text that reaches the shell.\n\nA regression test should invoke the target and assert it does not fail with a shell parse error. The existing coverage did not catch a 100% failure of the documented path, which is the more interesting gap.\n\n### Impact\n\n`AGENTS.md` names `make worktree name=<branch>` as the one-command path for the mandated fresh-worktree workflow, so every agent following the canonical guidance hits this on its first command.\n\nNo changes made and nothing claimed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789699492589146760,"uuid":"d9e909de-4dab-40b1-a48d-e50aabb4dada"}